# `optim::OptimaStallCategory`

A diagnosis of why a run stalled or ended without converging.

`OptimaOutput::stall_category` (and each progress snapshot) classifies the cause of a failed or cut-short run, so that a caller can decide what to do. `None` means no stall. `UserStop` is a progress hook stopping the run. `InvalidCallbackContract` means a callback returned the wrong shape or dtype. `NonFiniteCallbackRegion` means the objective or a constraint was NaN or infinite near the iterate. `SearchDirectionCollapse` means the step shrank to nothing. `BoundaryLimited` means progress is blocked by a bound. `InfeasibleStationary` means the point is stationary for the violation but infeasible. `ComplementarityStagnation` means the barrier or complementarity measure stopped improving. `FeasibilityFailure` means no feasible point was reached. `RecoveryFailure` means restoration or non-finite recovery failed. `IterationLimit` means the budget ran out. [`optima_stall_category_name`](optima_stall_category_name.md) names a value; `stall_measure` and `stall_reference` give the numbers behind the call.

## Fields

### `None`

`enumerator`, default `0`.

No stall.

### `UserStop`

`enumerator`, default `1`.

A progress hook stopped the run.

### `InvalidCallbackContract`

`enumerator`, default `2`.

A callback returned the wrong shape or dtype.

### `NonFiniteCallbackRegion`

`enumerator`, default `3`.

NaN or infinity near the iterate.

### `SearchDirectionCollapse`

`enumerator`, default `4`.

The step shrank to nothing.

### `BoundaryLimited`

`enumerator`, default `5`.

A bound blocks progress.

### `InfeasibleStationary`

`enumerator`, default `6`.

Stationary for the violation but infeasible.

### `ComplementarityStagnation`

`enumerator`, default `7`.

Complementarity stopped improving.

### `FeasibilityFailure`

`enumerator`, default `8`.

No feasible point reached.

### `RecoveryFailure`

`enumerator`, default `9`.

Restoration or recovery failed.

### `IterationLimit`

`enumerator`, default `10`.

Budget exhausted.

## Guidance

Read from `state.output.stall_category` or a snapshot.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

A run cut short by its iteration limit.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series target = pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0});
  const auto objective = [&](const pluss::Series &x) { return (x - target).square().sum(); };
  const auto disc = optim::constraints().nl_ineq([](const Pack &p) { return p.at("x").square().sum() - 1.0; });

  optim::OptimaOptions options;
  options.sequential_qp.max_iterations = 1;
  const optim::OptimaState result = optim::optima(objective, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), options, disc);
  out.writeln("stall =", optim::optima_stall_category_name(result.output.stall_category), ", measure =", result.output.stall_measure, ", reference =", result.output.stall_reference);
}
```

### Example 2

A hook stop.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series target = pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0});
  const auto objective = [&](const pluss::Series &x) { return (x - target).square().sum(); };
  const auto disc = optim::constraints().nl_ineq([](const Pack &p) { return p.at("x").square().sum() - 1.0; });

  optim::OptimaOptions options;
  options.progress_hook = [](const optim::OptimaProgressSnapshot &) { return true; };
  const optim::OptimaState result = optim::optima(objective, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), options, disc);
  out.writeln("stall =", optim::optima_stall_category_name(result.output.stall_category));
}
```

### Example 3

A converged run has no stall.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series target = pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0});
  const auto objective = [&](const pluss::Series &x) { return (x - target).square().sum(); };
  const auto disc = optim::constraints().nl_ineq([](const Pack &p) { return p.at("x").square().sum() - 1.0; });
  const optim::OptimaState result = optim::optima(objective, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), {}, disc);
  out.writeln("stall =", optim::optima_stall_category_name(result.output.stall_category));
}
```

